<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Getting started on vex</title><link>https://tyroncameron.github.io/vex/docs/01-getting-started/</link><description>Recent content in Getting started on vex</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-GB</language><atom:link href="https://tyroncameron.github.io/vex/docs/01-getting-started/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Installing vex</title><link>https://tyroncameron.github.io/vex/docs/01-getting-started/01-installing-vex/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tyroncameron.github.io/vex/docs/01-getting-started/01-installing-vex/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;vex is a single LuaJIT program with no services to run. Installing it means putting the &lt;code&gt;vex&lt;/code&gt; command on your path and, optionally, enabling shell completion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="requirements"&gt;Requirements &lt;a href="#requirements" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LuaJIT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clone of the vex repository.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="running-vex"&gt;Running vex &lt;a href="#running-vex" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;src/vex&lt;/code&gt; is the entry point (&lt;code&gt;src/vex.bat&lt;/code&gt; on Windows). It finds its own directory, sets up Lua&amp;rsquo;s module paths and runs &lt;code&gt;src/vex.lua&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="prism-codeblock vex-console"&gt;
&lt;button type="button" class="vex-console-copy" title="Copy commands" aria-label="Copy commands" onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(Array.from(this.parentElement.querySelectorAll('.vex-command'), e =&gt; e.textContent).join('\n')); this.firstElementChild.textContent = 'check'; setTimeout(() =&gt; this.firstElementChild.textContent = 'content_copy', 1500)"&gt;&lt;span class="material-icons"&gt;content_copy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="vex-command"&gt;&lt;span class="vex-program"&gt;git&lt;/span&gt; clone https://github.com/TyronCameron/vex.git&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="vex-command"&gt;&lt;span class="vex-program"&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; vex&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="vex-command"&gt;&lt;span class="vex-program"&gt;./src/vex&lt;/span&gt; help&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To run &lt;code&gt;vex&lt;/code&gt; from anywhere, link the wrapper onto your path:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Creating your first task using vex</title><link>https://tyroncameron.github.io/vex/docs/01-getting-started/02-creating-your-first-task-using-vex/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tyroncameron.github.io/vex/docs/01-getting-started/02-creating-your-first-task-using-vex/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This page walks through the core loop: &lt;code&gt;init&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;add&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;show&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;set&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;get&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;focus&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;resolve&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;remove&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="1-initialise-a-project"&gt;1. Initialise a project &lt;a href="#1-initialise-a-project" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="prism-codeblock vex-console"&gt;
&lt;button type="button" class="vex-console-copy" title="Copy commands" aria-label="Copy commands" onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(Array.from(this.parentElement.querySelectorAll('.vex-command'), e =&gt; e.textContent).join('\n')); this.firstElementChild.textContent = 'check'; setTimeout(() =&gt; this.firstElementChild.textContent = 'content_copy', 1500)"&gt;&lt;span class="material-icons"&gt;content_copy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="vex-command"&gt;&lt;span class="vex-program"&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; my-project&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="vex-command"&gt;&lt;span class="vex-program"&gt;vex&lt;/span&gt; init&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Task files go in the folder named by &lt;code&gt;taskfolder&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;.vex/config.lua&lt;/code&gt;. By default that&amp;rsquo;s the project root (see &lt;a data-bs-delay="{&amp;#34;hide&amp;#34;:300,&amp;#34;show&amp;#34;:550}" data-bs-html="true" data-bs-title="&lt;a href='https://tyroncameron.github.io/vex/docs/03-configuration/01-configuring-vex-config.lua/'&gt;&lt;p&gt;CONFIGURATION&lt;/p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Configuring vex (config.lua)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;`.vex/config.lua` returns a Lua table and is read on every command. `vex init` writes this one:&lt;/a&gt;" data-bs-toggle="tooltip" href="https://tyroncameron.github.io/vex/docs/03-configuration/01-configuring-vex-config.lua/"&gt;Configuring vex (config.lua)&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Using a recipe to create a sequence of tasks</title><link>https://tyroncameron.github.io/vex/docs/01-getting-started/03-using-a-recipe-to-create-a-sequence-of-tasks/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tyroncameron.github.io/vex/docs/01-getting-started/03-using-a-recipe-to-create-a-sequence-of-tasks/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A recipe is a named shortcut that creates one or more tasks with fields already filled in. Use one whenever you set up the same kind of work repeatedly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="listing-recipes"&gt;Listing recipes &lt;a href="#listing-recipes" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="prism-codeblock vex-console"&gt;
&lt;button type="button" class="vex-console-copy" title="Copy commands" aria-label="Copy commands" onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(Array.from(this.parentElement.querySelectorAll('.vex-command'), e =&gt; e.textContent).join('\n')); this.firstElementChild.textContent = 'check'; setTimeout(() =&gt; this.firstElementChild.textContent = 'content_copy', 1500)"&gt;&lt;span class="material-icons"&gt;content_copy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="vex-command"&gt;&lt;span class="vex-program"&gt;vex&lt;/span&gt; recipe&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="vex-output"&gt;Available recipes:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="vex-output"&gt; abstract&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With no name, &lt;code&gt;vex recipe&lt;/code&gt; lists the recipes available. vex ships &lt;code&gt;abstract&lt;/code&gt;, which creates a task of type &lt;code&gt;abstract&lt;/code&gt;: a parent that groups other tasks.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>